      "names": {
        "de": "Purmel",
        "en": "Scatterbug",
        "es": "Scatterbug",
        "fr": "Lépidonille",
        "it": "Scatterbug",
        "ja": "コフキムシ",
        "ko": "분이벌레",
        "ja-Hrkt": "コフキムシ",
        "zh-Hans": "粉蝶虫",
        "zh-Hant": "粉蝶蟲"
      },
      "description": {
        "fun": "Scatterbug happily munches poisonous leaves and roots, then turns the poison into a black powder that it dusts all over its body. The powder paralyses anything that touches it, keeping bird Pokémon away, and also lets it cope with any climate. Its squared-off specks look like confetti or screen pixels, a first hint of the pixel-patterned butterfly it grows into.",
        "guide": "Scatterbug is a Bug-type caterpillar Pokémon from Kalos. It eats poisonous plants and coats itself in the black powder it makes from them, which paralyses predators and protects it in any climate. It evolves into Spewpa and then Vivillon, whose wing pattern depends on where it comes from.",
        "tagline": "A caterpillar dusted in its own paralysing powder",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Scatterbug (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Scatterbug_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
