      "names": {
        "de": "Vivillon",
        "en": "Vivillon",
        "es": "Vivillon",
        "fr": "Prismillon",
        "it": "Vivillon",
        "ja": "ビビヨン",
        "ko": "비비용",
        "ja-Hrkt": "ビビヨン",
        "zh-Hans": "彩粉蝶",
        "zh-Hant": "彩粉蝶"
      },
      "description": {
        "fun": "Vivillon's wings change with the climate and landscape it was born in, giving 20 different patterns, from Meadow to Monsoon. In X and Y, the pattern you found depended on where in the real world your game was set, so collecting them all meant trading across the globe. The idea may come from Papilio dardanus, a butterfly with more than 14 forms, each mimicking a different species.",
        "guide": "Vivillon is a Bug- and Flying-type butterfly Pokémon, the final form of Scatterbug. Its wings come in 20 patterns shaped by the climate and terrain of its birthplace; in Generations 6 and 7 the pattern depended on the player's real-world location. The Meadow Pattern is the one usually shown in artwork.",
        "tagline": "A butterfly with 20 patterns, one for each corner of the world",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Vivillon (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Vivillon_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
